    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGQ2NzIzZGUyNzg0MzMzOTA4ZjAzNTc4MDFiMzM3ZWQyZmU5ZTVmYzY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-16T15:19:59Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-16T15:19:59Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(sim): calculate the playback stock removal before playback\n\nThe traced playback worker now cuts the whole program once when the\ntransport starts, and keeps keyframes of the cut stock at a fixed\nstride. A jump forward or back then restores the keyframe at or before\nthe playhead and cuts at most one stride, so playback no longer lags\nbehind a long jump.\n\n- Keyframes are held to a 512 MiB budget (at most 1024, at least 64\n  moves apart); past the budget the store thins and the stride doubles.\n- The transport shows the progress and a Cancel button. A cancelled,\n  stopped or refused calculation is \"incomplete\" by name; the moves\n  after the last keyframe are cut live.\n- The stamp is the document version: each command retires the worker\n  and frees its keyframes.\n- Display only: the Deviate verdict and the post gate are unchanged\n  (pinned).\n\nFixes #2181\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
